{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scene\/defaultposition(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that specifies where to place a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newly opened window relative to the screen bounds."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A scene that uses a default position for new windows."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first time your app opens a window from a particular scene"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration, the system places the window at the center of the screen by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default. For scene types that support multiple simultaneous windows, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system offsets each additional window by a small amount to avoid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"completely obscuring existing windows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can override the default placement of the first window by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applying a scene modifier that indicates where to place the window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to the screen bounds. For example, you can request that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system place a new window in the bottom trailing corner of the screen:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultPosition(.bottomTrailing)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The system aligns the point in the window that corresponds to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with the point in the screen that corresponds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the same unit point."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You typically use one of the predefined unit points — like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in the above example — but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can also use a custom unit point. For example, the following"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"modifier aligns the point that’s one quarter of the way from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leading edge of the window with the point that’s one quarter of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the way from the leading edge of the screen, while centering the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window in the y-dimension:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".defaultPosition(UnitPoint(x: 0.25, y: 0.5))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The modifier affects any scene type that creates windows in Windows,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"namely:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Window"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DocumentGroup","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Settings"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The value that you provide acts only as an initial default. During state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restoration, the system restores the window to the position that it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last occupied."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9Un